-- SITE-23 — Powell Butte has no polygon, so every home in it classifies as
-- "outside every boundary", Brasada Ranch included.
--
-- WHAT WAS WRONG. public.refresh_listing_boundary_tags() (migration
-- 20260823030000) stamps listings.boundary_city with the literal string
-- 'Outside Boundaries' when no geo_type='city' polygon contains the home's
-- point. That string is a SENTINEL, not a place: lib/slug.ts:203-217 and
-- app/listing/[listingKey]/listing-json-ld.ts:86-91 both refuse it as a URL
-- segment. Refusing it in the URL builder was the 2026-08-27 fix; it did not
-- touch the DATA, and the data is what every polygon-sourced figure reads.
--
-- Measured 2026-09-08 through lib/data/listings/getBoundarySentinelCoverage.ts
-- (exact counts, service role): 7,885 listings carry the sentinel; 180 of them
-- have MLS City 'Powell Butte'; 114 of those name Brasada Ranch as their
-- subdivision. Only 41 of 2,297 geocoded Brasada listings carry any
-- boundary_neighborhood at all.
--
-- TWO DEFECTS, both fixed here.
--
-- 1. COVERAGE. `boundaries` holds no row for Powell Butte at any geo_type.
--    Broad check first, per the absence rule: `geo_label ilike '%powell%butte%'
--    OR geo_slug ilike '%powell%butte%'` across ALL geo_types returned zero
--    rows, while the same shape returned the Brasada Ranch neighbourhood row,
--    so the query works and the absence is real. Powell Butte is also not a
--    Census PLACE: TIGERweb Incorporated Places (layer 4) and Census
--    Designated Places (layer 5) both return zero for NAME LIKE '%Powell%' in
--    state 41, and an envelope query over the Brasada area on layer 5 returns
--    no CDP at all — while a control query for Tumalo returns its CDP. It is
--    an unincorporated community, so the authoritative Census geometry for it
--    is the COUNTY SUBDIVISION: Powell Butte CCD, GEOID 4101392550, Crook
--    County (013), MTFCC G4040, AREALAND 374,154,738 m2 = 144.46 sq mi. That
--    is the polygon inserted below, verbatim from TIGERweb at SRID 4326 — not
--    hand-drawn, not buffered, not a hull (feedback_gis_authoritative_only).
--    A CCD is a statistical DIVISION of a county: they tile the county and do
--    not overlap each other, so this cannot fight Prineville's or Redmond's
--    city polygon, and the classifier picks the smallest containing polygon
--    per geo_type anyway.
--
-- 2. A STICKY SENTINEL. The Brasada Ranch neighbourhood polygon already
--    existed and is sound — valid, 1.388 sq mi, Crook County GIS Subdivisions
--    — and all three test coordinates below fall INSIDE it, yet those rows
--    carry boundary_neighborhood = NULL. The reason is the RPC batch filter:
--    `WHERE boundary_city IS NULL`. Once a row is stamped it is never looked
--    at again, so a polygon that lands LATER never reaches the homes it
--    covers. The Brasada polygon was re-sourced on 2026-08-26; the rows had
--    been stamped long before. The comment on the original said the sentinel
--    exists "so the queue does not retry forever", which is a real concern —
--    so the fix is not to retry forever but to retry ONCE PER CHANGE to the
--    boundary set. A new boundary_tagged_at column carries when a row was last
--    classified; a sentinel row becomes eligible again exactly when
--    `boundaries` has gained a row since. Clean rows are never revisited.
--
-- Verification traces are in the SITE-23 commit body.

-- 1 ---------------------------------------------------------------- coverage

